  "text_summary": {
    "layer": "text",
    "body": "On the third day Esther put on royal clothing and stood in the inner court; the king held out the golden scepter and offered her up to half the kingdom. She invited the king and Haman to a banquet, and there to a second banquet the next day. Haman left joyful, but seeing Mordecai at the gate neither rise nor tremble, he was filled with fury; at home he boasted to Zeresh and his friends of his wealth and honours, yet said all was worth nothing while Mordecai sat at the gate. They advised a gallows fifty cubits high and a request for Mordecai's death in the morning; he had it made.",
    "passage": "Esth.5.1-Esth.5.14"
  },
